Players can explore events on the current grid by consuming energy, and completing events will reward players with prizes. There are three types of events:
1) Wild Monsters: encounter monsters of different strengths, players can choose to fight or bypass them, and win battles to gain rewards and exploration points;
2) Pokemon Egg Event: The system will generate a specified number of Pokemon eggs based on the number of participants. It will reset and refresh at 9, 12, 16, and 19 o'clock daily. When encountering a Pokemon egg during the exploration, players can choose to bypass or add it to their backpack. After holding the egg for 120 seconds, it can be manually hatched, and hatching the egg will reward players with exploration points;
3) Battle Encounter Event: When exploring the current grid, players will encounter other guild players in the same grid, and can choose to bypass or fight against them. If the player wins the battle, they will gain corresponding battle points and take the Pokemon egg carried by the opponent's backpack. To take the egg, players need to have an available slot in their backpack. The backpack can only hold a maximum of 4 Pokemon eggs, and if there are not enough slots, players cannot take the egg.

